---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Insurance & Advertiser Disclosure — QuoteShield"
  description="QuoteShield Insurance & Advertising Disclosures. Clear explanation of our data sources, editorial independence, rate benchmarks, and regulatory status."
>
  <div class="page-header">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="badge badge-trust">Transparency & Compliance</span>
      <h1>Insurance & Advertiser Disclosures</h1>
      <p class="subtitle">Our commitment to regulatory transparency, factual accuracy, and consumer protection.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="container page-content article-content">
    <div class="callout callout-warning">
      <div class="callout-title">⚠️ Important Consumer Notice</div>
      <p class="callout-text">
        QuoteShield is an independent publisher of consumer education, rate benchmarks, and insurance research. QuoteShield is <strong>not an insurance carrier, agency, underwriter, or licensed insurance producer</strong>. We do not sell insurance policies, underwrite risk, bind coverage, or adjudicate insurance claims.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2>1. Data Sources & Rate Benchmarking Methodology</h2>
    <p>
      The insurance rates, premium averages, savings figures, and coverage comparisons presented on QuoteShield are derived from:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Public rate filings submitted by insurers to state insurance commissioners and departments of insurance;</li>
      <li>Aggregated databases provided by the National Association of Insurance Commissioners (NAIC);</li>
      <li>Publicly available tariff sheets and regulatory market conduct examinations;</li>
      <li>Hypothetical standard consumer profile models (e.g., 35-year-old driver with clean record, 2023 sedan, standard limits).</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      <strong>Rates are illustrative only.</strong> Insurance premiums are highly personalized. Your actual rate will be determined exclusively by the underwriting insurer based on individual variables including your specific credit-based insurance score, exact residential address, motor vehicle record, claims history, annual mileage, vehicle identification number (VIN), marital status, and selected deductibles and coverage limits.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Advertiser Disclosure</h2>
    <p>
      QuoteShield is a free resource for consumers. To support our editorial research, server infrastructure, and expert review board, we may receive compensation from companies whose products or services are featured or linked across our platform.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Commercial Relationships:</strong> When you click on certain links to obtain a quote or purchase a policy from a third-party insurer, we may earn an affiliate commission or referral fee.</li>
      <li><strong>Editorial Independence:</strong> Compensation does not dictate our carrier star ratings, editorial critiques, or rate analysis methodologies. Our editorial team (including licensed CPCU, CFP®, and CLU professionals) evaluates carriers using objective metrics regardless of commercial arrangements.</li>
      <li><strong>No Endorsement:</strong> The inclusion of an insurer or quote option on our website does not constitute an official endorsement, warranty, or guarantee of policy performance or claims payment.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. State Insurance Department Notice</h2>
    <p>
      Insurance requirements and minimum mandatory coverage levels vary substantially by state jurisdiction. While we strive to maintain up-to-date statutory references across all 50 states, state legislatures and insurance commissioners frequently update statutory minimums and no-fault tort thresholds. Consumers are encouraged to verify current legal minimums with their respective state insurance commissioner's office.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Health & Medicare Disclosures (CMS Compliance)</h2>
    <p>
      QuoteShield is not connected with or endorsed by the U.S. government or the federal Medicare program (Centers for Medicare & Medicaid Services - CMS). Any Medicare-related content is published strictly for educational clarity to help beneficiaries understand the distinctions between Original Medicare (Part A and Part B), Medicare Advantage (Part C), Medicare Part D prescription plans, and Medicare Supplement (Medigap) plans.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Inquiries & Feedback</h2>
    <p>
      If you represent a state regulatory body or insurance department with questions regarding any published rate reference, please direct correspondence to our compliance division at <a href="mailto:legal@quoteshield.online">legal@quoteshield.online</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-header {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #0c1e33 0%, #153252 100%);
    color: #ffffff;
    padding: 3.5rem 0 3rem;
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }

  .page-header h1 {
    color: #ffffff;
    font-size: 2.5rem;
    margin: 1rem 0 0.75rem;
  }

  .subtitle {
    color: #cbd5e1;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .page-content {
    max-width: 860px;
  }
</style>
